# Build & Test Convention

## Before Every Commit
1. Set JAVA_HOME: `export JAVA_HOME=/Users/vkannan/Library/Java/JavaVirtualMachines/ms-21.0.8/Contents/Home`
2. Run: `cd backend && ./mvnw clean test -B`
3. ALL tests must pass — never commit with failures
4. Check for spec drift on any config/constant change

## Java Environment
- Java 21 LTS (Microsoft OpenJDK) — NOT Homebrew Java 24 (causes SSL issues)
- Maven 3.9.9 via Maven Wrapper (./mvnw)
- Test DB: H2 in-memory (application-test.yml, Flyway disabled)

## Test Location
- Unit tests: `backend/src/test/java/com/artha/unit/`
- Integration tests: `backend/src/test/java/com/artha/integration/` (Testcontainers)
- Test naming: `{Subject}Test.java` (e.g., `CashFlowServiceTest.java`)

## Frontend (when Node.js is available)
- `cd frontend && npm run build` — TypeScript compilation must pass
- `cd frontend && npm test` — Vitest tests must pass
